              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**\"Still in Love with You\"** is the closing track (Track 10) on Brooks & Dunn\u2019s multi-platinum debut studio album, ***Brand New Man***, which was released on August 13, 1991. \n\n### Key Details About the Song:\n* **The Songwriters:** The track was co-written by **Kix Brooks**, **Ronnie Dunn**, and their frequent collaborator/producer **Don Cook**.\n* **Lead Vocals:** Unlike many of the duo's biggest radio hits from that album (such as \"Neon Moon,\" \"Brand New Man,\" and \"Boot Scootin' Boogie,\" which feature Ronnie Dunn on lead), **Kix Brooks sings lead vocals** on \"Still in Love with You\". \n* **The Theme:** It is a melancholy, bittersweet ballad about a painful departure. The narrator is leaving their lover, sitting in a waiting taxi, and heading toward Baton Rouge, while hoping their memory lingers enough to bring them back together.\n\n### Notable Lyrics:\n> *My taxicab's waiting*\n> *Wish I could hold you one last time*\n> *After all we had together*\n> *There's gotta be a better way*\n> *Of telling you goodbye*\n>\n> *If I had a horse*\n> *I'd ride off in the sunset*\n> *If I had wings, I'd fly off*\n> *In the sky so blue*\n> *If I had the time, I'd spend my*\n> *Whole life dreaming*\n> *But I'd wake up, still in love with you...*\n\nThough it was never released as a radio single, \"Still in Love with You\" remains a fan-favorite deep cut that showcases Kix Brooks' softer, more earnest vocal delivery.",
